Tenali Rama and the Brinjal Curry (Raw Story)

id: WBX_100098

One day, King Krishnadevaraya tasted a delicious brinjal curry in the royal kitchen.

He loved it so much that he ordered the cook to prepare it often.

Tenali Rama also tasted the curry and enjoyed it a lot.

That evening, he told his wife about the tasty dish.

His wife said, “I would love to taste it too!”

Tenali decided to bring some brinjals from the royal garden.

At night, he quietly went into the garden and plucked a few brinjals.

The next day, the king noticed that some brinjals were missing.

He was angry and ordered everyone to find the thief.

Tenali knew he might get caught, so he made a clever plan.

He told his young son, “If anyone asks you what you ate last night, say you had brinjal curry.”

Later, in court, the boy was asked.

He said, “I ate brinjal curry in the rain last night!”

But it had not rained at all.

The king realized the boy was confused and dismissed the matter.

Tenali smiled, and no one suspected him.

💖 Moral:

Quick thinking can save you from trouble.
